- Session 2026-08-15: Messenger-style multi-bubble floating chat stack (native + JS). Rewrote `ChatBubbleService.kt` from a single bubble to a `LinkedHashMap<String, BubbleEntry>` stack (MAX_BUBBLES=4) keyed by participantKey; all bubbles share a drag position (stackX/stackY) and fan out vertically (BUBBLE_STEP_DP=8); tap opens that bubble's conversation; tapping a different bubble while the window is open switches; long-press + ✕ dismisses one; 5th conversation auto-replaces the oldest. Fixes the stale-avatar bug (reopening a conversation now repaints its avatar). New `ACTION_HIDE_ONE` + per-bubble `setUnreadCount(key, count)`; `ChatBubbleModule.kt` gained `hideOne(key)` + `setUnreadCount(count, key)`. JS: `activeBubbleConversations` Map, `getActiveBubbleConversations()`, `hideBubble(key?)`, `setBubbleUnreadCount(count, key?)`; ChatList badge sync loops over all bubbles. New unit suite `ChatBubbleService.test.ts` (8 tests). tsc clean; unit 52 suites / 538 tests green. Changelog updated. UNCOMMITTED — requires Android rebuild to verify on device.
- Session 2026-08-15: Floating chat window background-open load fix (native). The floating chat overlay is a ReactSurface on the same ReactHost as the main activity; when the app is backgrounded, RN's onHostPause() freezes the JS timer pipeline (JavaTimerManager removes the Choreographer callback), so a window opened by tapping the bubble over another app stuck on the loading spinner (FloatingChatContent waits for DB-ready via a setInterval poll + theme + queries) until the user returned to the app. FIX in `android/app/src/main/java/ai/soulbits/chat/ChatBubbleService.kt`: `openFloatingChat()` calls `forceResumeHostForOverlay()` before `surface.start()` (checks `host.lifecycleState != RESUMED` → `host.onHostResume(lastResumedActivity)` 1-arg overload); `closeFloatingChat()` calls `restoreHostPauseAfterOverlay()` which pauses the host (no-arg `onHostPause()`) ONLY if we force-resumed AND the app activity isn't foreground (`isAppActivityResumed` tracked via activity lifecycle callbacks + initialized from `host.lifecycleState` in `onCreate`). `onActivityResumed` clears `hostResumedForOverlay` so closing after returning to the app never pauses a foregrounded host. Side-effects verified harmless (AppState 'active' emission; EntitySessionService only reacts to 'background'; double-pause idempotent). No JS changes. Requires Android rebuild to verify. Changelog updated (Chat & Messaging > Fixed). UNCOMMITTED.
