- Session 2026-08-03: Sync size-estimate confirmation + toast suppression (uncommitted — user to decide commit split; engine repo changes uncommitted too).
  - Engine estimate correctness (harmony-link-private, TDD): shared `whereChangedSince`/`whereChangedSinceNoDeletedAt` predicates in `database/sync_utils.go`; `CountChangedRecords(tx, table, sinceTimestamp)` (table-name switch for 2-col `emotion_state`), `CountChangedCharacterImages(tx, ts)` (count+bytes); `sendSizeEstimate` covers all 33 tables, image-count error handled, `EstimatedDownloadMB` computed before logging. Root cause: bare `strftime('%s',...)` returns TEXT → SQLite compares TEXT vs INTEGER watermark by storage-class ordering ("TEXT > any INTEGER") → estimate over-counted (7 claimed vs 0 sent). Tests: 3 DB + 2 eventserver integration (estimate==actual), `go build` + `go test ./database/ ./eventserver/` green.
  - Estimate confirmation protocol: new engine event `SYNC_DATA_SIZE_ESTIMATE_CONFIRM`; `sendLocalChanges` registers a `PendingConfirms` channel and blocks until the app confirms (SUCCESS → proceed; REJECTED/timeout → `SYNC_REJECT` + abort, no data transmitted). Engine `SizeEstimateConfirmationTimeout = 60s`. App: `SyncService.handleSizeEstimate`/`confirmSizeEstimate`/`pendingSizeEstimate` + `sync:estimate`/`sync:estimate:confirm` events; themed dialog via `useAppAlert` (AppAlertProvider reordered ABOVE SyncConnectionProvider in App.tsx). Mock server `setSendSizeEstimate(true)` + `setEstimateDownloadMB(mb)`.
  - CRITICAL snake_case fix: engine estimate payload JSON tags are snake_case (`estimated_download_mb`/`total_records`/`image_count`) but app + mock server used PascalCase → production dialog would never appear. Fixed reads, mock emission, and tests (assert PascalCase key is `undefined`).
  - Toast suppression: `shouldShowConnectionErrorToast` gate in `syncSettlementHelper.ts`; wired into `SyncConnectionContext` (handleSyncError + connect catch, `isCertFlowActiveRef`) and `ConnectionSetupScreen.handleConnectionError` (`showCertModalRef`). Suppresses misleading "connection error"/"connection dropped" toasts during the expected pairing/TLS/cert handshake. Follow-up (on-device logcat 08-03): a FOURTH ungated path remained — `handleHandshakeAccepted`'s catch fired "Failed to establish connection" because `attemptSecureConnection` rethrows non-cert InsecureSSL errors (raw RN WS event → `isCertError` string check fails; self-signed lib emits plain `'error'`, not `cert:verification_failed`). Fixed with the same gate there (certFlowActive always true during pairing → suppressed); new scenario test in `syncSettlementHelper.test.ts`. REFACTOR (same session): extracted the copy+pasted gate wiring into `shouldShowConnectionErrorToastForConnection` (async, DI getters `getConnectionInfo`/`getSecurityMode`; new `SyncConnectionMode` type alias) used by all 4 sites; i18n'd ConnectionSetupScreen's 11 hardcoded toasts to `t('...')` (connection ns; added missing `failedToEstablishConnection` key). Verification: tsc clean; unit 28 suites / 333 tests; integration 8 suites / 31 + 1 skip.
  - Confirmation threshold: `shouldPromptForSyncEstimate` pure helper (new `src/contexts/syncEstimateHelper.ts`); default 5 MB, `null`="Unlimited" → never prompt, empty → auto-confirm, `isInitialSync` → always prompt. Persisted via `ConnectionStateManager.getSyncEstimateLimitMB()/setSyncEstimateLimitMB()/clearSyncEstimateLimitMB()` (AsyncStorage key `sync_estimate_limit_mb`). `SyncSettingsScreen` dropdown (1/5/10/20/50/100/Unlimited) via `SelectPicker` + i18n.
  - Verification: `tsc --noEmit` clean; unit 28 suites / 333 tests (incl. 6 new connection-toast-helper tests + handshake-catch toast-gate scenario); integration sync suite 31 pass + 1 skip (syncService 14 incl. estimate accept/reject/backward-compat/configured-size).
- Session 2026-08-02: Sync-race fix + sync-watermark wipe reset + legacy alias removal (uncommitted — user to decide commit split).
  - Sync-race fix (Complete, TDD): `syncSettlementHelper.isSyncTransportSettled` gate in `SyncConnectionContext.handleSyncConnected` (defer auto-sync on provisional ws:// until transport settles); `SyncService.abortSync()` + `sync:aborted` event wired to `disconnected:sync`/`error:sync`/`sync:connection_replaced`; `ConnectionManager` emits `sync:connection_replaced` before teardown; `handleSyncComplete` awaits `sendLocalChangesSequentially`; `SyncSettingsScreen` resets spinner on abort. Root cause: auto-sync on provisional connection + ws→wss upgrade teardown mid-sync → orphaned `currentSession` ('in_progress' forever, "Sync already in progress, skipping"). Tests: syncSettlementHelper (9 unit) + sync.abort (3 integration). On-device logcat verified gate + abort firing, no stuck state.
  - Sync-watermark wipe reset (Complete, TDD): `ConnectionStateManager.clearAllLastSyncTimestamps()` clears per-source keys on full wipe — called from `wipeDatabaseCompletely` AND `clearDatabaseData`. Root cause: wipe left `last_sync_timestamp:selfhosted`/`:cloud` in AsyncStorage → next sync incremental vs recent ts → 0 records ("no data during sync").
  - Legacy alias removal (Complete, Option B): dropped `last_sync_timestamp` global key entirely — `getLastSync` no legacy fallback, `setLastSync` no dual-write, constant deleted, both Settings screens read per-source via `getCurrentSource()`. Single source of truth. Tests updated: connectionStateManager.lastSyncReset (7), syncService.integration + sync.clock seeds cleaned, timestamp-completion test asserts legacy key NOT written.
